abstract: "A curated, standardized collection of empirical phylogenetic datasets covering taxonomic groups across Bacteria, Archaea, and Eukaryota. Organized into 62 partitions yielding 264 standardized trees (26 partition-canonicals + 218 Condamine family-level + 20 sub-clade), with tip-label normalized Newick trees, a global standardized-label dictionary, full label mappings, and metadata. Companion to the manuscript 'Where the tree of life is empirically resolved, and where it is not: an open atlas of species-level phylogenies and their archival uncertainty' (Richter, 2026, under review)."
